# NOTES #

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-1]  Registration is required for certain tasks, such as editing protected pages, creating pages on the English Wikipedia, and uploading files.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-2]  Most text is also dual-licensed under  [LINK: (GFDL) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Free_Documentation_License] ; media licensing varies.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-3]  Pronounced  [LINK: (/ˌwɪkɪˈpiːdiə/) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English]   [LINK: (ⓘ) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:En-uk-Wikipedia.ogg]   [LINK: (WIK-ih-PEE-dee-ə) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Pronunciation_respelling_key]  or  [LINK: (/ˌwɪki-/) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English]   [LINK: (ⓘ) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-Wikipedia.ogg]   [LINK: (WIK-ee-PEE-dee-ə) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Pronunciation_respelling_key]  in  [LINK: (English) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_language]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-32]  Available as an archive at the  [LINK: (Nostalgia Wikipedia) -> https://nostalgia.wikipedia.org/wiki/]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-109]  Revisions with libelous content, criminal threats, or copyright infringements may be removed completely.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-159]  The committee may directly rule that a content change is inappropriate, but may not directly rule that certain content is inappropriate.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia#cite_ref-289]  See "Libel" by David McHam for the legal distinction.


