"Dark Side of Wikipedia". Full Measure. Archived from the original on August 4, 2016. Retrieved April 17, 2016.  [LINK: (Full Measure with Sharyl Attkisson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Full_Measure_with_Sharyl_Attkisson] , April 17, 2016. (Includes video.)

Wales, Jimmy (December 9, 2016). "How Wikipedia Works".  [LINK: (Cato Institute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cato_Institute] . Jimmy Wales, founder of Wikipedia, discusses the site, how it's treated by governments, and how it's fueled by its users.

The Great Book of Knowledge, Part 1: A Wiki is a Kind of Bus,  [LINK: (Ideas, with Paul Kennedy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ideas_(radio_show)] ,  [LINK: (CBC Radio One) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBC_Radio_One] , originally broadcast January 15, 2014. The webpage includes a link to the archived audio program (also found here). The radio documentary discusses Wikipedia's history, development, and its place within the broader scope of the trend to democratized knowledge. It also includes interviews with several key Wikipedia staff and contributors, including  [LINK: (Kat Walsh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Walsh]  and  [LINK: (Sue Gardner) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sue_Gardner]  (audio, 53:58, Flash required).

"So Is Wikipedia Cracking Up?" The Independent, February 3, 2009.

Wikipedia's Year-End List Shows What the Internet Needed to Know in 2019. Alyse Stanley, December 27, 2019, Gizmodo.

